WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.200
Usually, when I come to Estonia,

2
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.440
I'm in complete shock
for the first week.

3
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:17.840
I cry, I'm jet-lagged,
I'm all messed up.

4
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.080
I walk around the streets of Tallinn.
I'm so tired.

5
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.480
It's usually very cold.
The weather in Estonia is as it is.

6
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.680
Emotion is taken to the extreme.

7
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.960
Then I start to quietly come out of it

8
00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.880
to figure out what I'm
really thinking or feeling.

9
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.880
Then I think that
my home is in America.

10
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.520
Why does coming to Estonia have to be
like tearing open a wound every time?

11
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.120
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

12
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.640
THE TEARS OF TWO HOMES

13
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.800
It's a bit hard for me
to go to Estonia.

14
00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.400
I know that when we leave,

15
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.920
everyone will be very sad
that we're leaving again.

16
00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.120
Although we only came to visit.

17
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.680
But I see that
everyone is starting to...

18
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.080
The wounds are tearing open
that we're gone.

19
00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:24.200
I always feel guilty and very sad

20
00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:30.440
that I have to hurt everyone again
by leaving again.

21
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:35.920
This is the main thing I always
think about when I go to Estonia,

22
00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:41.080
that there will be such a difficult
moment at the end.

23
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:46.760
I always think that
I'll come to Estonia and rest.

24
00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.480
I don't have to work.

25
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.600
But in the end,
you're like the prime minister,

26
00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.560
that everyone comes to see you.

27
00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.320
One hour with this person,
another hour with another person.

28
00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:03.120
Like that all the time
and in the end you're just so tired.

29
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.120
And then half the people are offended
that you didn't see them.

30
00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.600
I always think of all the things I want
to do in Estonia while I'm in Dubai.

31
00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.360
All the food I want to try,

32
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.080
all the places I definitely want to go
or all the friends,

33
00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.720
then I always agree on everything
at the beginning of the trip.

34
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.520
And the more time goes by,
the more I realize that

35
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.280
I can't do all these things.
There's just so much to do every day.

36
00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:49.680
I always think that
now comes the travel FOMO.

37
00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.880
I try to sleep very little
while I'm in Estonia

38
00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:59.240
so I can get more things done
that I have on my mind.

39
00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:04.760
There's just so much to do in Estonia

40
00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.720
and you value
these things more because

41
00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.400
you can't get them here.

42
00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.560
I just have two homes.

43
00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.960
When I'm in one, I miss the other.

44
00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:30.840
Once, we spent
the whole summer in Estonia.

45
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.520
We came from Canada,
took the summer off,

46
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.240
and were in Estonia
for about four months.

47
00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.880
We had such a great time that

48
00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.720
until the last minute,
on the way to the airport,

49
00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:46.160
we were talking about whether
we should even get on the plane.

50
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.920
We have such a great time at home.
Why are we leaving?

51
00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.840
When we got to our Canadian home,
we had a great time there too.

52
00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.760
Why did we even think about
not leaving?

53
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:05.120
It's like...

54
00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:10.720
Two homes, both are in my heart,
both are great.

55
00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:15.160
I don't feel torn between the two.

56
00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:18.720
I just feel like I'd like to
visit Estonia more often.

57
00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.520
I looked at my
Norwegian airline account

58
00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:33.640
and saw that I've travelled
42 times in the past year.

59
00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:40.440
That means to Estonia and back,
back and forth, 22 times in Estonia.

60
00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:45.160
Contact with Estonia is so close,

61
00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:49.160
these trips are so habitual.

62
00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:56.040
If we were to create a scale
and say what is most important,

63
00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:59.920
what is most attractive about Norway,

64
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.560
it would be the geographical location.
It is simply so close.

65
00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:13.440
We have such frequent
and good air traffic with Estonia,

66
00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.240
it's easy.

67
00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:27.160
I lived in New York
and I felt like a New Yorker.

68
00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.520
When I'm in Paris,
I feel like a Parisian.

69
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.680
When I lived in Chicago,
for example...

70
00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:40.000
The places you've been longer,
you feel more like a local.

71
00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:43.800
I lived in New York for four years
and I feel at home there.

72
00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:49.040
I've also been in Paris
for about four years

73
00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.840
and I feel at home there.

74
00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.720
I always feel at home in Tallinn.

75
00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.760
However, in all these places
I feel a bit out of place.

76
00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:01.840
There are always some practices
that seem foreign.

77
00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:08.760
I have noticed that sometimes
I may have an identity crisis.

78
00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:16.000
I have a sense of belonging
to both Estonia and Switzerland.

79
00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.040
Especially when I travel to Estonia,

80
00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:26.000
I get homesick for Switzerland.

81
00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:30.960
And in Switzerland
I feel a longing for Estonia.

82
00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:35.080
Sometimes I don't understand

83
00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:40.760
which cultural space or environment
I actually belong to more.

84
00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:47.240
I think I'm more comfortable
in Austria.

85
00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:52.800
I like the anonymity and the freedom

86
00:06:53.640 --> 00:07:00.000
to be free and searching,
no matter how old you are.

87
00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.560
I think

88
00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:09.160
I feel more at home in Austria.

89
00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.560
Despite everything
that is foreign to me there.

90
00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:24.640
When I visit Estonia,
I don't feel like I'm visiting.

91
00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:31.680
It's more like I'm going home,

92
00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:37.840
because that's where my home is too.

93
00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:45.480
There's such excitement
when we go to Estonia.

94
00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.960
I'd like to show my children
and my husband

95
00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:53.440
as much as possible
what's good about Estonia.

96
00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.520
When I come back to Dubai,

97
00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:11.920
when I see the Dubai towers and
the city lights from the plane window,

98
00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:16.520
it doesn't make me feel like home.

99
00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:22.880
I can't even explain
the feeling I have.

100
00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:27.600
Confusion -
I think that's the right word for it.

101
00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:33.760
It's not home, but it is.

102
00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:43.200
It's hard to explain, this feeling,
but it's kind of oppressive.

103
00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:47.040
And it's not like...

104
00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:53.520
You know deep down that
this is not a home forever.

105
00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:59.600
Makes you wonder if it's worth it
to come back here.

106
00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:06.120
Is it worth it to be away
from your family and friends.

107
00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:15.480
I can't talk anymore,
I'm starting to cry again.

108
00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:39.640
You'll have to ask our families
how they see it, but...

109
00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:44.960
As much as we see and experience,
it is very difficult.

110
00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:49.560
Well, they're not happy that
we're here abroad.

111
00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:56.680
And when we said we're coming
back to England for the second time,

112
00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:59.680
it was a terrible shock to them.

113
00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:03.600
They thought we were done
with this phase of our lives.

114
00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:06.760
That we have been there, done that.

115
00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:10.120
So that's it,
and when we came back again,

116
00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:13.360
it turned their lives
completely upside down.

117
00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:18.040
That's something they still
haven't really forgiven us for,

118
00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.520
or they haven't come to terms with.
- Absolutely not.

119
00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.600
Will they ever?
- I believe they will.

120
00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.000
They get used to it?
- Maybe, or not.

121
00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:30.280
It will probably take time.

122
00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:36.120
It's not easy for us to come here
and leave them there like that.

123
00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:41.000
I cried the same way here,
seeing my parents unhappy there.

124
00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.640
Yes, of course.

125
00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:47.280
That's the hardest part
of this whole thing so far.

126
00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:52.440
It tears you apart, and then I think,

127
00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:58.200
is it right for me
to do this to my family?

128
00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:00.760
Am I a good person?

129
00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:08.720
Maybe I should, I don't know,
throw my dreams away

130
00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:11.200
and go there and...

131
00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.160
Back to Estonia?
- Yes.

132
00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:31.960
When I visit Estonia,
I'm always very happy.

133
00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:36.640
I see familiar places,
I see familiar people, my family.

134
00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:42.600
It all creates a simple feeling
that I can be free.

135
00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:46.400
The other side is that
every time I visit,

136
00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:50.640
something has changed in Estonia,
something is different.

137
00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:55.040
I have to catch up
to keep up with everyone else.

138
00:11:55.120 --> 00:12:01.080
A new building, a new restaurant,
new customs, something's emerged again.

139
00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:04.840
I have this feeling that
I always have to catch up.

140
00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:09.240
Otherwise I don't know if I'm
truly Estonian enough,

141
00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:13.240
if I'm becoming an Estonian expatriate?

142
00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:20.680
Your 2-year-old baby doesn't care
where he nibbles grass.

143
00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:23.960
But as they get bigger and smarter...

144
00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:25.960
My son is ten.

145
00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.240
I think it's getting harder and harder

146
00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:31.960
and I'm also mentally preparing
myself for the moment

147
00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:34.960
when he says he doesn't want
to come to Estonia,

148
00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.160
because he's bored and has no friends.

149
00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:42.200
That's a big problem for me.
So will I come alone?

150
00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:48.120
I have a nice summer house in Põlvamaa,
I really like being here.

151
00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:52.920
Would I want to be here alone, leaving
my wife and children in America?

152
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.200
No, I really wouldn't.

153
00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:58.600
A few days maybe,
but what am I doing here alone?

154
00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:05.680
These are the little fears
and I don't know a good solution.

155
00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:13.680
On the other hand, every summer
the children hear signals

156
00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:18.240
about how they don't belong here
one hundred percent.

157
00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.280
Because we get compliments like,

158
00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:24.480
wow, you speak like pure Estonian!

159
00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:28.440
Well... of course, I'm Estonian,
what do you mean?

160
00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:32.200
Nobody tells an Estonian,
"You speak Estonian really well."

161
00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.800
Of course I do, I'm Estonian!

162
00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.720
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

163
00:13:38.320 --> 00:13:40.320
THE TEARS OF TWO HOMES

164
00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:04.760
Translated by Piret Õunapuu
